## Agents DIY vs Service

- Cost: DIY looks free until you count engineer hours building Slack bots, schedulers, and status pages, incident.io's per-seat pricing is cheaper than one engineer's month.
- Lock-in: lives in Slack or Teams you already use, exports your data, standard API and Terraform provider, nothing tricky to unwind.
- Reliability: your homegrown pager is a single point of failure with no one paging you when it breaks, incident.io is battle-tested infra with its own on-call.
- Coverage: on-call scheduling, escalations, response, AI investigations, insights, and status pages in one platform, a DIY stack needs 5 tools stitched together.
- Maintenance: no bot to patch, no cron jobs to babysit, no integration drift, they ship improvements weekly while you ship your product.
- AI out of the box: automated investigations, PR drafting, and noise reduction you'd never build in-house.
- Learning loop: insights and post-incident analysis built in, DIY setups capture incidents but never learn from them.
- Signup is the whole setup: go to incident.io/free-trial, start the free trial, connect Slack in a couple of clicks, first incident channel in minutes, demo at incident.io/demo if you want a tour.
